Zeo patch 0003 — a model's default OAuth MCP tools follow the user's real connection, and never redirect a new chat.

Target: Open WebUI v0.11.4 (ghcr.io/open-webui/open-webui:v0.11.4).
Applied by ai/openwebui/Dockerfile.openwebui with `patch -p1` from /app.

Upstream: opening a new chat on a model whose default tools include an
OAuth 2.1 MCP server (e.g. Phoenix) the user has not connected sends the
browser straight to /oauth/clients/mcp:<id>/authorize, and blocks sending
until the integration is connected. Users the MCP server does not authorise
land on its "not authorised" page on every new chat.

This patch filters OAuth MCP tool ids out of info.meta.toolIds in the
GET /api/models response, per user, unless the user is really connected:
a token (oauth_client_manager.get_oauth_token, the same call GET
/api/v1/tools derives `authenticated` from) AND the MCP server accepts it
(an `initialize` sent with the headers a real tool call sends). Connected:
the tool is on in every new chat. Refused (401, or 403 invalid_token): the
token is renewed once and retried; a second refusal deletes the session, so
the Integrations menu shows "connect". No answer (timeout, 5xx, 429): off for
now, session kept, back on by itself when the server answers. Verdicts are
cached 60 s (accepted) / 15 s (otherwise) per user and access token, and
concurrent page-load lookups share one check, bounded at 6 s. Response only
— model rows are never changed.

It also makes OAuthClientManager.get_oauth_token refresh single-flight. The
chat layout fetches /api/models and /api/v1/tools together on every page
load, and both look the token up; upstream refreshed an expiring token once
per caller with the same refresh token, a server that rotates refresh tokens
refused all but the first, and the losers deleted the session the winner had
just renewed. That is why a user with valid credentials found the tool off
after every access-token expiry. Now one refresh runs per (user, client), the
rest reuse its result, and a session is deleted only when it can never be
renewed (the token endpoint answers 400/401, or the token has expired with
no refresh token). A transient refresh failure keeps the session. A
non-refreshable token is served until it really expires instead of being
deleted five minutes early.

Backend only on purpose: the upstream image ships the Svelte frontend
pre-compiled, so patching Chat.svelte would mean rebuilding the bundle.

Files: backend/open_webui/main.py,
       backend/open_webui/utils/oauth.py,
       backend/open_webui/utils/mcp_oauth_defaults.py (new).
See ai/openwebui/OPENWEBUI.md § MCP tools (Phoenix) and § Custom image.

